<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Deliberately the same colours as values/styles.xml, and that is not an
         oversight.

         These themes dress the window the system shows before any of this
         app's code runs, so the only thing they can key off is the *device's*
         dark mode. But the app carries a theme of its own, it defaults to
         Light, and the two are independent: a shopper with a dark phone who
         never opened Account settings then Theme is running a Light app.
         Keying the launch window off the device painted #1B2229 for the whole
         engine and Dart start-up and then cut to a light app, measured here at
         roughly 3.2s of dark on a debug build, and that is the "black screen"
         being reported. Matching the device was the wrong target. Matching the
         app is the right one, and the app's default is light.

         A shopper who did choose Dark is not left on a light window: that is
         the case MainActivity handles, repainting the ground from the saved
         preference right after super.onCreate(). It cannot help before the
         process exists, which is exactly why the static colour here is the
         app's own default rather than the device's. -->
    <style name="LaunchTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/launch_background</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">#F3F2F2</item>
    </style>
    <style name="NormalTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">?android:colorBackground</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">#F3F2F2</item>
    </style>
</resources>
